### 3. CAO ..YUAN `@littlecrawler` (3 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2113-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/8" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Does the order of Level and extension tags matter?**
</div>

 Hi, I would like to clarify the expected tag order when a Level has a required extension.

  For example, for Level-4 and A-Inheritance, should we:

  1. tag the working non-inheritance implementation as Level-4, then implement inheritance and tag it as A-Inheritance; or
  2. complete and tag A-Inheritance first, then tag a later commit as Level-4, so the Level-4 state includes the required extension?

Does the order of a Level tag and its required extension tag matter, or can we place them in either order as long as both increments are completed and tagged correctly?

</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2113-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/6" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2. :fas-info-circle: Clarification on commits and tags for iP increments**
</div>

 Hi Prof/Teaching Team, I would like to clarify the expected commit and tag workflow for an iP increment.

  If an increment is completed through several logical commits, should we squash them into one commit and tag that commit, or keep the commits
  separate and place the increment tag only on the final commit that first completes all requirements?

  In the latter case, are the earlier commits since the previous increment tag considered part of the same increment?

  Thank you!
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2113-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/5" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**3. :fas-info-circle: Clarification on updating an earlier increment after tagging it**
</div>

Hi Prof/Teaching Team,

I would like to clarify how updates to earlier increments should be handled.

Suppose I complete Level-1, tag the corresponding commit as Level-1, and push both the code and tag. While working on Level-2, I later improve or modify some functionality originally implemented for Level-1. I then complete the Level-2 requirements and tag the latest cumulative version as Level-2.

Could you please clarify:

Is it acceptable for the Level-2 version to contain both improvements to Level-1 functionality and the new Level-2 functionality?

Should the existing Level-1 tag remain pointing to the original Level-1 completion commit?

If the later change fixes a missing Level-1 requirement rather than being an optional improvement, should the pushed Level-1 tag be updated, or should it remain unchanged?

Thank you!

</panel>

</panel>


